# Enforce CRLF line endings on Windows batch files — cmd.exe cannot parse LF-only .bat files
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never convert line endings (2026-10-14, v9.3.0 update failure).
# With core.autocrlf=true git guesses text vs binary by looking for zero bytes.
# The HR Portal PDFs use ASCII85-encoded streams (no zero bytes), so git treated
# them as text and stripped their CRs on commit -- GitHub then served different
# bytes from the ones update_manifest.json hashed, and every in-app update to
# v9.3.0 failed the integrity check on those PDFs. Declaring the types binary
# makes git store and serve the exact bytes. Keep in step with _BINARY_EXTS in
# scripts/release.py (tests/unit/test_release_binary_attrs.py checks it).
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.exe binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls binary
*.docx binary
*.doc binary
*.pptx binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
